<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kexholm</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Käkisalmi, Priozersk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kexholm, in Finnish Käkisalmi and today Priozersk in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, is a town and fortress on the Vuoksi river near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a>, which gave its name to the surrounding province of Kexholm. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> won the town and province from Russia by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stolbovo">Treaty of Stolbovo</a> in 1617 and held them until the Great Northern War, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> took the fortress in 1710; the cession was confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nystad">Treaty of Nystad</a> in 1721.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kexholm.jpg" alt="Kexholm" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tvkosone · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%A4kisalmen_tori_23.10.2016.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
